sions (0o600) for SQLite database file.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-378\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"IMMEDIATE: Implement authentication (JWT or API key) for all endpoints. Require valid credentials on websocket and REST API connections.\",\n    \"IMMEDIATE: Fix CORS configuration. Change allow_origins=['*'] to specific trusted domains or require Origin header validation.\",\n    \"IMMEDIATE: Validate GEMINI_API_KEY at application startup, not just log a warning. Fail fast if missing.\",\n    \"HIGH: Implement input validation on WebSocket query_text. Use Pydantic schemas to validate all user input.\",\n    \"HIGH: Never expose exception details to clients. Implement error handlers that log full details but return generic messages.\",\n    \"HIGH: Add rate limiting to REST endpoints using middleware (e.g., slowapi or similar).\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Use comprehensive URL parsing (urllib.parse or similar) instead of regex for URL normalization.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Set restrictive file permissions on SQLite database (mode 0o600) to prevent unauthorized file access.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Consider implementing request signing or HMAC verification for API calls if this system becomes public-facing.\",\n    \"LOW: Update User-Agent header to accurately identify the client, or use a generic non-browser identifier.\",\n    \"LOW: Add security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Strict-Transport-Security) to HTTP responses.\",\n    \"REVIEW: Audit all LLM prompts for prompt injection vulnerabilities. The orchestrator prompt includes user queries directly.\",\n    \"AUDIT: Review policy_registry.json for hardcoded secrets or sensitive information.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n**Risk Score: 72/100 (High)**\n\nThe most critical issues are:\n\n1. **No Authentication** — All endpoints are publicly accessible\n2. **CORS Misconfiguration** — Accepts requests from any origin\n3. **Environment Variable Validation** — API key validation